  "summary": "Recent preprints connect superconductivity with spin-to-charge conversion, quantized transport and thermometry in nanoscale devices.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the coupling of superconducting phase coherence to charge, spin and thermal transport in nanoscale devices. A gate-tunable superconducting quantum point contact in Ge/SiGe, probed with a SQUID, shows correlated quantization in conductance and switching current. A moiré flatband superconductor in alternating twisted trilayer graphene is linked to quantum phase fluctuations between superconductivity and bosonic phases. A two-orbital quantum dot Josephson junction with Rashba spin-orbit coupling and Zeeman splitting is proposed to convert a temperature difference into a phase difference for thermometry. A theoretical proposal argues that the inverse spin Hall effect in a superconductor could approach unity spin-to-charge conversion in a nonlocal spin-valve geometry. All four items are preprints, and the multiorbital and spin-conversion items are theoretical proposals.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
